{"nodes": [{"id": "entity_total_trim_correction_delta_b2", "label": "total_trim_correction_delta_b2", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "research/chunks/ecu-diagnosis/07_comparative-signature-tables.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Emitted by OBDLab but read nowhere in comlab non-test code - the symmetric/asymmetric bank discriminator (strongest internal-vs-external tell) has no consumer. ECU-FU-2 closes this orphan: add the consumer, do not add a field."}, {"id": "entity_bank_symmetry", "label": "bank_symmetry", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "research/chunks/ecu-diagnosis/07_comparative-signature-tables.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "External sensor/harness faults are typically bank-specific; internal faults touching a shared plane (reference ground, VREF) hit both banks symmetrically. B1-vs-B2 symmetry is a primary discriminator."}, {"id": "entity_deceptive_lambda", "label": "deceptive_lambda", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "research/chunks/ecu-diagnosis/07_comparative-signature-tables.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Single-cylinder coil/injector faults pump raw fuel + raw O2 in stoich proportion, so lambda_chem ~1.01 looks normal while HC ~2200 ppm screams misfire. Never clear a fault on lambda alone - read HC and O2."}, {"id": "entity_o2", "label": "O2", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "research/chunks/ecu-diagnosis/07_comparative-signature-tables.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "entity_comparative_signature_tables", "label": "Comparative Signature Tables (Tables 1-3)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "research/chunks/ecu-diagnosis/07_comparative-signature-tables.md", "sourc